WEBVTT

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.490
Now, facing the Champion Makunouchi is a former gymmate he once trained with, Hammer Nao.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.950
But there's no hint of familiarity in their eyes!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.400
They're clearly meeting as enemies!

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.730
Ippo looks a lot tougher than usual.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.290
That just means he's focused!

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.740
You think he'll go all out at the start?

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.670
Do you seriously think he'll be able to hit him?

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.170
We'll know soon enough.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.300
Then I guess we'll see what happens after the bell rings.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.800
Now both competitors head for their corners.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.380
The odds are 9 to 1.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.340
The crowd is pretty certain of Makunouchi's victory.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.060
I wonder if things will really be that easy.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.400
It'll be an extremely close range battle, so the Dempsey Roll can't be used.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.000
Ippo-kun is bound to get hit a few times when they fight it out.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.080
They trained together,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.400
so I'm sure they have a good grasp on each other's fighting styles.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.390
How much has the gap shrunk in the last two years,

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.410
or has it widened?

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.970
The key lies in how they spent that time...

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.460
and what kind of progress they made.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.540
This fated reunion...

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.800
The fated bell...

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.470
But what fate will await them at the conclusion of this match!?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.290
Makunouchi is a slow starter!

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.300
So take the initiative and try to set the pace!

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:25.960
Right!

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.070
<i>I'm warmed up, so I can go at any time.</i>

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.960
<i>The second the bell rings, and we've touched gloves, I'll come out swinging!</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.730
<i>I'm going to take the advantage early, senpai!</i>

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.770
Don't think about playing it defensive just because you're the champion!

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.720
Stay on the offensive!

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.620
Right!

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.320
<i>That's what I intend to do.</i>

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.020
<i>I'll give it my all.</i>

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.120
<i>That's the answer I have for Yamada-kun who made me his goal.</i>

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.210
Box!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.590
And there's the bell.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.110
This reunion after two and a half years...

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.210
what kind of greeting will it be?

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.630
Whoa, the champion dashes in!

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.510
He slides past the hand that was extended to touch gloves and attacks!

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.080
A left hook!

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.400
The challenger is pushed to the ropes in an instant!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.910
It's a berserker barrage!

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.150
The champion is out to crush the challenger from the start!

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.480
That's far too vicious to chalk up as tough love; the champion is on the warpath!

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:24.930
A sidestep!

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:28.740
The challenger wants to regroup and is able to escape the ropes!

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.750
But a right chases after him!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.500
The challenger is knocked down sideways!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.710
Nao!

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.800
A down already!

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.230
An explosive right!

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.220
Thirty seconds after the start of the match!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.760
The Champion Makunouchi is already showing us the pride of a senpai!

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.200
H-He did it.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.920
I guess we didn't need to worry about whether or not he could hit him.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.600
Those shots were all fully loaded!

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.440
He passes.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.090
Aoki?

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.300
If he can pull off something like that, then he's made the cut.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.490
I hereby designate Ippo an underdog hunter.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.530
Quit talking big!

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.240
I thought you were gonna teach him how to polish off people who don't stand a chance!?

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:09.810
ONE

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.190
Now the count begins.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.750
TWO

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.490
Will the challenger be able to stand,

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.490
THREE

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:16.750
or will it end right here?

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.230
FOUR

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.760
The champion looks down as if to make clear the difference between their levels!

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:19.850
FIVE

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.620
I've never seen Makunouchi look that scary before.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.300
I bet he's pissed off that his kouhai was acting so high and mighty!

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.270
SIX

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.030
<i>T-That really hurt.</i>

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.200
<i>But that's no surprise.</i>

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.220
<i>I took the full force of one of senpai's punches.</i>

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.330
<i>I was knocked down before I even knew what was going on.</i>

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.290
<i>And I was supposed to be the one on the offensive.</i>

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.610
<i>Is this the difference in our experience?</i>

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.980
SEVEN

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.660
<i>But I knew all of that.</i>

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.680
<i>I was prepared for this much!</i>

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.300
He's standing and takes his fighting pose!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:58.790
Box!

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.050
Whoa, the champion doesn't hesitate to go on the assault!

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.300
The challenger doesn't get a chance to catch his breath!

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.310
Stick to him!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.140
Even if it's a clinch, just hang in there!

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.140
It's a clinch!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.680
The challenger attempts to buy some time and rest!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.850
But the champion forces them apart!

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.840
The champion is different today!

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.100
It almost seems as if he's angry!

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.200
It's like they're brawling.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.150
I've never seen Makunouchi-senpai like that before.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:31.890
Nao!

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.490
He'll go after you again if you try to run!

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.270
Push him back!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.420
A left that seems to push the champion away!

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.790
It's a swing that could give you goose bumps!

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.350
<i>That was close!</i>

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.590
<i>I almost hit him!</i>

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.540
The champion regroups and regains his balance.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.100
The wave of attacks seems to have stopped.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.370
<i>That's right.</i>

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.780
<i>If I just punch, he's close enough for me to hit him.</i>

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:56.890
<i>So fight back!</i>

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.190
The challenger makes an aggressive push!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.650
His heavy looking punches keep the champion at bay!

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.140
<i>He's within my range!</i>

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.300
<i>If I keep punching, then I'll definitely be able to hit him!</i>

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.950
<i>If I keep punching...</i>

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.420
So many punches are being thrown that it's hard to believe he was just down!

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.330
But none of them are connecting!

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.330
The champion continues to brilliantly head slip even at this super-close range!

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.040
<i>H-He's fast!</i>

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.960
<i>He's even faster than he was two years ago!</i>

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.090
<i>It should be possible to hit him when he's this close, but I can't!</i>

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.340
<i>There's too much of a difference in our speeds!</i>

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.720
A desperately thrown left ends up falling prey to a right counter!

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.720
And now the champion moves in!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.140
A fearsome rush!

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.150
It's thrown relentlessly on top of his guard!

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.450
A-Amazing.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.230
I know this guy is cannon fodder, but is the difference really this big?

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.960
He looks really pissed.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.410
He really plans on wiping him out.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:58.280
I-It's kind of scary.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.320
Is that really Ippo?

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.990
I can understand wanting to put the screws to a stuck up kouhai,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.530
but he could show a little mercy.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.300
That's Ippo all right.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.130
But scary?

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:13.890
All I see...

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.610
All I see...

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.690
in his face is desperation.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.050
<i>I'll give it everything I've got!</i>

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.450
<i>But I want...</i>

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:29.190
<i>I want this to end as soon as possible!</i>

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:30.900
A right!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.790
The challenger's knees buckle!

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.370
That got him!

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.330
The champion goes in for the finish!

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.580
He retaliates!

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.040
A left!

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.330
But it's pushed aside!

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.590
A left!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.840
A right!

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.780
D-Damn.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.340
What a ruthless assault.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.280
<i>I don't want the match to last any longer!</i>

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.840
<i>I don't want to keep doing this!</i>

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.850
<i>I have to end it!</i>

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.170
He's fallen!

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.110
A second down!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.330
Get to a neutral corner!

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.930
The champion heads to a neutral corner!

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:17.070
It must have been a truly devastating shot!

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:16.450
ONE

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.370
He doesn't look back!

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:18.420
TWO

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.110
The challenger isn't moving!

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.210
THREE

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.370
Is there even a need for a count!?

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.050
FOUR

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.800
Did that do it!?

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.200
No doubt about it.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.460
Taking a clean punch like that from Ippo...

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.880
it's a one way ticket to unconsciousness.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.170
<i>There was incredible feedback.</i>

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.720
<i>I can still feel it in my hand.</i>

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.180
<i>The sensation of hitting Yamada-kun.</i>

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.880
<i>But it's all over.</i>

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.300
<i>He can't stand up after that one.</i>

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.840
<i>Now...</i>

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.690
H-He stands up!

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.110
SIX

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.190
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.740
N-No way.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.910
Forget unconscious, he got up during the ten count!

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.410
SEVEN

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.470
The count continues!

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.080
Will he be able to take his fighting pose!?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.580
<i>End it, referee.</i>

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.660
<i>Please end the match!</i>

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.460
<i>I don't want to hit him anymore!</i>

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.230
<i>I still haven't...</i>

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.470
<i>haven't done anything.</i>

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.720
<i>Stop it.</i>

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.720
<i>I'm not going...</i>

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>not going to let it end like this!</i>

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:27.940
Box!

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.480
It continues!

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.550
But if he falls again, it'll be the third down!

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.280
The match will officially end!

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.490
The challenger has no room for mistakes!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.990
And the champion has plenty of time to finish him off!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.700
<i>About one minute left...</i>

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.320
<i>I have to finish this!</i>

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:47.250
<i>If I knock him down again, it'll be over!</i>

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.250
<i>I can end this!</i>

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.000
The champion flies out from the neutral corner!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.340
Go, Makunouchi!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.620
Give us a first round KO!

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:57.080
Show us a big finish!

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:02.050
<i>I'm meeting the senpai I idolize in the ring.</i>

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.890
<i>I can't let it end without doing something!</i>

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.010
<i>I won't let it end!</i>

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.350
The peek-a-boo style!?

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.610
The challenger tightens his guard!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.360
The champion fires away in spite of it!

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.080
He's on a fierce attack!

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.320
Can he put an end to this match?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.780
<i>The match will end if I can pry open his guard and drill him with a big one!</i>

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.880
Looks like Ippo's not that naive.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.570
He's gonna wrap it up!

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.290
No, he's definitely naive.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:33.130
He's in too much of a hurry to finish it off.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.860
He's been throwing flashy punches, but only with his arms.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.290
Even the punch he got that down with

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:42.050
came from just swinging his arms and only using upper body strength.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.380
I see,

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.480
so if Ippo's weight had been behind that punch, he wouldn't have been able to get up.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.370
Too much of a hurry?

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.560
But he's doing so well.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.910
He's being too straight forward.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.570
Compare that to what Gero-michi's doing.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.110
That's...

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.600
...Operation Turtle!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.960
Tightening your guard and biding your time until your opponent lets his guard down.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.330
It's something Ippo uses a lot when he's got his back against the wall.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.580
Right,

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:15.460
Ippo always finds a way to make a comeback after using that!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.020
Gero-michi...

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.340
has a plan.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.020
<i>He's so fast that I can't follow him.</i>

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.550
<i>At this rate, I'm doomed!</i>

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.590
<i>If there's nothing else I can do,</i>

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:28.100
<i>I might as well use my best punch!</i>

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.690
A body blow from the challenger!

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:37.230
But the champion saw it coming! It's blocked solidly!

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:40.240
Whoa, the champion's legs are lifted into the air!

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:41.490
Did you see that shot to the body!?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.240
He flew at least ten centimeters off the ground!

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.620
<i>That wasn't a featherweight punch.</i>

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.740
<i>I could tell it was a punch from a higher weight class!</i>

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.420
<i>He blocked it?</i>

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.160
<i>But he was dodging everything else.</i>

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.540
<i>That's it!</i>

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.080
<i>If I had been calmer, I would have realized...</i>

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.350
<i>no matter how quickly he moves his head,</i>

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.370
<i>his body doesn't move!</i>

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.670
<i>That's it!</i>

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:08.640
<i>Aim for his body!</i>

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:12.660
Another body blow from the challenger that connects!

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:15.650
Two! Three!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.520
A sudden counterattack! The champion winces in pain!

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.540
<i>It's working! I can hit him!</i>

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.280
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.540
<i>Don't back down!</i>

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.530
<i>Fight back!</i>

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.270
It's turned into a slugfest!

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:27.280
Has the challenger chosen to risk it all!?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.560
30 seconds remain!

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.560
Will he be finished off!?

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.790
Will he survive!?

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.800
Both fighters connect!

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.460
Less than 20 seconds left!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:39.030
<i>I'm able to hit senpai with my punches.</i>

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.050
A left!

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.650
Did that get him!?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.540
Will he fall!?

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:46.700
<i>No way will I fall!</i>

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.430
<i>I can finally hit him!</i>

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:49.920
<i>Just a little more!</i>

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.360
<i>It's only just begun!</i>

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:52.670
<i>It's just getting started.</i>

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.060
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.610
<i>Why are you stopping it, referee?</i>

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.470
That's the bell!

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:00.820
Didn't you hear it?

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.760
The first round is over.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.070
Go back to your corner.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.080
What a strange sight!

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:21.590
The one looking disappointed was not the champion who failed to finish things,

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.460
but the challenger!

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:25.970
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.150
<i>It was just getting good.</i>

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:29.860
<i>Next time...</i>

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.300
<i>In the next round...</i>

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:44.400
The first round was almost the final round, with two downs having been scored.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.670
With a score of 10-7, the senpai, Makunouchi, has the undisputed lead.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:53.910
What will happen in the next three minutes of this battle between former gymmates?  {Word check on gym mates}

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.690
After I was finally able to hit him...

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.420
When I was just getting started...

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:00.860
Nao...

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.140
Did you see, Coach?

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.350
My punches actually hit senpai!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.900
You bet I did.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.590
Aiming for the body was a good decision.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:13.140
Your body blows are first rate goods, heavy and effective!

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:16.230
Land enough of them and you'll definitely win!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.300
All right,

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:19.910
I'm going for his body in the next round too!

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.790
I'll keep hitting him there and after I land enough...

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.190
After I land enough...

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.180
You've realized it?

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:30.720
Body blows take a while before they start to have an effect.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:37.180
You have almost no chance of being able to land enough if you keep getting hit by Makunouchi.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:39.980
His punches are just too powerful!

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.340
But my other punches won't connect!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.820
He's too fast and I can't catch him.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:48.880
What should I do?

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:52.520
I don't want this to end in the early rounds.

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:55.700
I still haven't shown him anything.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.350
Don't give up yet.

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:03.580
There is a body blow...

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.360
that takes immediate effect.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:06.890
It's called...

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.900
the Solar Plexus Blow.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.660
You know why you couldn't beat him?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.840
I got carried away and threw too many punches.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.750
And when I was open from throwing too many big punches, he fought back.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.500
And do you know why you were throwing too many big punches!?

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:34.510
I anticipated him putting up a fight, but after those two downs, I thought I could end it in that round.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.370
It looks like I need to teach you what it means to be a pro.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.020
What it means to be a pro?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:44.080
You do the job you're given.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.450
You answer the audience's expectations.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:48.520
And one more thing...

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.280
You devote yourself to the fight!

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:57.130
If you can't accomplish these three things,

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.620
then you can't call yourself a true pro boxer!

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.540
Let alone call yourself the champion!

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.220
Keep that in mind when you get out there!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.070
Yes! {jama: added}

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.550
And now the second round.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.600
Get him, Makunouchi!

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.930
Don't let him drag this out too long!

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.550
Wrap it up in this round!

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:21.060
The crowd seems more concerned with how Makunouchi will win rather than if he will win.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:25.060
They face off in a seemingly mirror match as both competitors use the peek-a-boo style.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:29.070
Will it be the expected outcome or an unseen upset?

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.090
Both fighters rush forward!

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.780
They're in so close that their heads could collide!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.740
Their feet are astride!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.790
A sign that neither intends to back down!

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:42.320
A left to the body!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:43.290
Safely blocked!

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:45.630
A right to the body!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:46.540
Also blocked!

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.650
The champion saw it coming!

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:49.630
He's seen through you!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.550
Your body blow plan is clear as day!

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:57.580
<i>He anticipated the plan for body blows after the exchange at the end of the last round.</i>

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:59.430
<i>He's experienced all right.</i>

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:05.230
The champion makes the challenger stagger with a single shot!

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.850
The challenger insists on body blows!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.230
But the champion's block grows sharper!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.700
<i>I may have given Nao useless advice.</i>

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.910
<i>Solar Plexus...</i>

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:24.990
<i>A strike to the pit of the stomach that will disrupt a person's breathing right away.</i>

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:29.630
<i>If he can pull off that fast-acting body blow, Makunouchi will stop moving.</i>

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.820
<i>But with that heavy duty block there's no way a body blow...</i>

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.260
<i>is making it through there.</i>

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>Am I making Nao waste his time?</i>

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.490
He's missing a lot more.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:48.190
After using so many body blows, it's no surprise that he sees them coming.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.150
A persistent attack to the body!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.650
But it comes up empty!

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.940
The champion fires back with precise blows!

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.420
Hammer, what are you doing!?

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.590
The same thing over and over again won't work!

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.320
Those shots to the body aren't going to hit anything!

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.580
<i>I have the timing and angle of his swing down.</i>

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.950
<i>I should be able to hit him as he pulls back his fist after he punches.</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.790
<i>He's even dodging the body blows now.</i>

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:11.460
<i>Just when I think I have a chance, he figures out a way of dealing with it.</i>

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.750
<i>But senpai,</i>

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.970
<i>how do you think an underdog like me made it this far?</i>

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.220
<i>Okay, when he pulls this punch back in,</i>

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.720
<i>I'll step in and nail him!</i>

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:30.850
<i>There's a way that even an underdog...</i>

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.110
<i>can take a bite out of someone!</i>

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:38.610
<i>Your solar plexus is wide open!</i>

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:44.200
A left to the body!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.620
It sinks in deep!

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.430
W-What's this body blow?

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.130
I can't breathe.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.160
<i>I-It landed!</i>

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.660
<i>The Solar Plexus Blow...</i>

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.590
G-Get him, Nao!

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.140
The challenger lays it on!

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.810
D-Damn it, Gero-michi! That's dirty!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.180
He faked missing the punch...

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:10.390
...and used his hand to pry open the guard.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:13.530
<i>I had to learn how to do things underhandedly...</i>

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.400
<i>if I wanted to make my way to the top!</i>

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.860
<i>Sorry, but I'm going to make the most of this opportunity, senpai!</i>

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:22.530
The challenger is fighting back as if to repay all his frustration!

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:24.240
<i>He got me!</i>

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.410
<i>It looks like I need to teach you what it means to be a pro.</i>

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:31.620
<i>You devote yourself to the fight!</i>

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:35.670
<i>Yamada-kun has devoted himself to this fight far more than I have.</i>

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.920
<i>He's a true pro boxer!</i>

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.930
The challenger uses his body blow as a lead-in and switches to the head!

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.680
The champion is pushed back!

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:47.680
This is the first time the champion has been pushed back in this match.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.650
Nao, keep at it!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.650
It's getting to him!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.680
You can beat him!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.200
A one-two!

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.440
It lands cleanly!

00:18:58.340 --> 00:18:59.740
But the challenger pushes forward!

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:02.110
He uses his advantage in size and pushes in!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:05.360
And another persistent attack to the body!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.610
The champion tightens his guard!

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:11.370
<i>The swing's too wide, dodge it!</i>

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:13.870
A razor sharp right body blow!

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.220
But it's dodged!

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.130
<i>He got me again!</i>

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.010
A left body blow explodes!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:29.290
You can see the impact through the champion's back!

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:34.690
This single shot causes the champion to freeze up and the challenger continues onwards!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.580
Damn it, he did it again!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:39.150
Referee, he's using his palms!

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:43.070
He's making such small motions to do it that the referee isn't catching it.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:43.900
Damn it all!

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:47.090
If there's no warning issued, then it can't be counted as a foul!

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:50.910
As long as the fight isn't stopped, then it's justified!

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.500
If anything, I'd commend him on it.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.330
But it's against the rules!

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:59.880
He's clearly using his hands, not his fists.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.890
But he hasn't had the foul called.

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:06.430
It's a technique that Hammer Nao has invented to survive in the ring.

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.420
Doing whatever it takes to win...

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.810
Arguably, the purest type of professional!

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.430
If I was his second, I wouldn't stop him from doing it.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:18.240
Hammer Nao is sharp.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.440
And the kid is dull!

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:26.700
And the champion is finally pushed to the corner!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.700
The kouhai has pushed his senpai to the brink!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.700
<i>Senpai...</i>
